ENTRY            M0120   20261016   20261127   20261127       M149
SUBENT        M0120001   20261016   20261127   20261127       M149
BIB                 12         38
TITLE      Nucleonic branches of the decay of the giant dipole
            resonance 0f Al-27.
AUTHOR     (U.R.Arzibekov,A.S.Gabelko,M.Kh.Zhalilov,K.M.Irgashev,
            B.S.Ishkhanov,I.M.Kapitonov,I.M.Piskarev)
REFERENCE  (J,SNP,40,713,1984)
            Eng. trans. of YF,40,1121,1984
           (J,YF,40,1121,1984)
INSTITUTE  (4RUSMOS)
FACILITY   (BETAT,4RUSMOS)
INC-SOURCE (BRST)
METHOD     (EXTB,SITA)
DETECTOR   (GELI) 100-cm**3 Ge(Li) detector
PART-DET   (G) Gamma detection at 140 deg.
COMMENT    Measured the gamma-spectra from
            Al-27(gamma,xgamma')Mg-26 and
            Al-27(gamma,ngamma')Al-26 reactions induced by
            bremsstrahlung gamma-quanta with 32-MeV end-point
            energy. The detection angle was 140 degrees.
            Integral cross sections of photonucleon
            reactions on Al-27 with formation of final nuclei
            in separate states are determined.
           The results are interpreted making use of the state
            population data from one-nucleon-transfer reactions.
           Conclusions are derived concerning the mechanism of
            photonucleon reactions and the part of isospin in
            the formation and decay the giant resonance of the
            Al-27 nucleus and of some other 1d2S-shell nuclei.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistical errors only.
HISTORY    (19860122C)
           (19910202A) Corrected by V.Varlamov, V.Mclane
           (20121101U) SD: Updated to new date formats,lower case.
                Corrected according last EXFOR rules and Dict.
                Ref. on transl. was added.
                       VV: STATUS.
           (20220213A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: AUTHOR
            (M.Kh.Zhalilov), COMMON, REACTION, PART-DET, STATUS.
           (20261016A) Corrected by V.Varlamov: TITLE, REFERENCE,
            PART-DET, REACTION, DATA, STATUS.
ENDBIB              38
COMMON               2          3
ANG        EN-MAX
ADEG       MEV
   140.       32.
ENDCOMMON            3
ENDSUBENT           45
